# Copy this file to .env. Git ignores .env, so your token stays on your PC.
#
#   copy .env.example .env      (Windows; then: notepad .env)
#   cp .env.example .env        (macOS and Linux)
#
# The horus program reads this file from the repo root. An environment variable
# with the same name wins over the file. Only the download code (horus
# download-model, which horus workflow install calls) reads HF_TOKEN. horus never
# prints the token and never puts it on a command line.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HF_TOKEN: your Hugging Face access token (required to download the models).
#
# The FLUX 3 Image Klein model is "gated". Hugging Face gives the files only to
# an account that accepted the license.
#
# 1. Sign in at https://huggingface.co (create a free account if needed).
# 2. Open https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy
#    Read the FLUX Kommunity License and accept it. Without this step every
#    download fails with HTTP 403, even with a valid token.
# 3. Open https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens and create a token of type
#    "Read". A Read token is enough.
# 4. Paste the token after the equals sign. No quotes, no spaces.
#
# HTTP 401 = the token is missing, wrong or expired.
# HTTP 403 = the token is valid, but its account has not accepted the license.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HF_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths (optional). Remove the # in front of a line to use it.
# Use full paths. Big models can live on any drive.
#
# The install folder of ComfyUI. ComfyUI itself is in its ComfyUI subfolder.
# Default on Windows: %USERPROFILE%\ComfyUI_windows_portable
# Default on macOS: ~/horus (no line is needed there)
# HORUS_COMFYUI_DIR=D:\ComfyUI_windows_portable
#
# Base folder for model files. It holds the subfolders diffusion_models,
# text_encoders, vae and so on.
# Default: <HORUS_COMFYUI_DIR>\ComfyUI\models
# HORUS_MODELS_DIR=E:\AI\models
#
# Only the text encoder folder, when it must be on another drive.
# horus workflow install then adds it to ComfyUI's extra_model_paths.yaml.
# Default: <HORUS_MODELS_DIR>\text_encoders
# HORUS_TEXT_ENCODER_DIR=E:\AI\models\text_encoders
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
